// The constitution gives the colors, the layout and a black five-pointed star, nothing else.
// From elsewhere, Album des Pavillons 2000 by way of FOTW's Heimer: about 1:2, the red
// stripe a third of the length, the stripes equal. On a 6 by 12 grid:
//   red 4 wide, yellow and green 3 high each
//   star in a circle of 1/3 hoist centered on the red: radius 1 at fly 2, hoist 3
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Guinea-Bissau"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  source "https://www.constituteproject.org/constitution/Guinea_Bissau_1996"
  source "https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/gw.html"
  note "The constitution read is the 1984 text as revised in 1996. A new constitution was reported approved, on provisional results, in a referendum of 30 August 2026, and its text wasn't found, so whether it restates this article is unconfirmed."
  note "The constitution gives no proportion or sizes. The 1:2 and the construction are the Album des Pavillons 2000 as FOTW reports it, which calls the ratio approximate. The star's size is a FOTW contributor's reading of that sheet. The Album itself wasn't read."
  note "The 1973 constitution, as FOTW quotes it, made the three stripes equal in area. The 1984 text no longer says so, though this construction still satisfies it."
  note "The colors are the Album des Pavillons 2023 as FOTW reports it. FOTW found no official shade. Black is plain black."
  law "Constitution of the Republic of Guinea-Bissau, Article 22, as revised 1996" {
    source "https://www.constituteproject.org/constitution/Guinea_Bissau_1996"
  }
}
palette {
  red "#c8102e" {
    pantone "186 C"
    cmyk 14 100 79 4
  }
  yellow "#ffcc00" {
    pantone "116 C"
    cmyk 0 21 93 0
  }
  green "#009530" {
    pantone "355 C"
    cmyk 84 12 100 1
  }
  black "#000000"
}
proportion hoist=6 fly=12

bars yellow green
panel {
  side hoist
  width 4
  field red
  charge star black {
    radius 1
  }
}
